    "body": "## Motivation\n\nDiffusion workers bind to their GPU's NUMA node (#43565). Many Kubernetes pods block the NUMA memory-policy syscalls, because they run without `SYS_NICE`. On those pods `_is_numa_available()` returns False, and the worker skips binding entirely:\n\n```\nUser lacks permission to set NUMA affinity, skipping NUMA node configuration for GPU.\n```\n\nCPU affinity (`sched_setaffinity`) needs no privilege, so the worker could still bind its CPUs. With CPUs bound, first-touch allocation keeps host memory on the node too. srt's V2 path already falls back this way (`--membind` → `--preferred` → CPU only), but the mempolicy gate in `_is_numa_available` returns before that fallback can run.\n\nOn a 2x GB300 pod without `SYS_NICE` (rx gb300-tml, GPU0 on node 0, GPU1 on node 1), the unbound FLUX.1 TP2 workers drift between sockets, and the request latency is bimodal (sample spread up to 60%).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `get_numa_node_if_available(..., cpu_only_ok=False)` and `_is_numa_available(require_mempolicy=True)`: the defaults keep srt's behaviour unchanged. With `cpu_only_ok=True`, a host where only CPU affinity can be set still returns the GPU's node, and logs that only CPUs are bound.\n- `numa_bind_to_node`: calls `numa_set_preferred` only when memory policy is permitted. The `sched_setaffinity` step is unchanged.\n- The diffusion GPU worker passes `cpu_only_ok=True`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo numerical change. This only changes the CPU affinity of the worker process.\n\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\n\nFLUX.1-dev 1024², TP2 eager, on the 2x GB300 pod without `SYS_NICE`. The two servers were interleaved; each value is the median of five requests, with the sample spread in parentheses.\n\n| | main | this PR (CPUs bound) |\n|---|---|---|\n| a. main `6576e50` vs the same change applied by hand, 2 rounds | 6.015 (26%), 6.440 (60%) | 5.547 (8%), 5.310 (6%) |\n| b. main `d0a098b` vs this commit, 2 rounds | 5.298 (12%), 5.118 (5%) | 5.189 (5%), 5.348 (6%) |\n| c. main `d0a098b` vs this commit, 4 more rounds | 5.411 (12%), 5.483 (7%), 5.153 (20%), 5.459 (14%) | 4.741 (7%), 5.474 (5%), 5.277 (12%), 4.833 (11%) |\n\n- **Binding:** the log confirms it now happens on this pod: `GPU 0 worker bound to NUMA node 0`, `GPU 1 worker bound to NUMA node 1`, `binding CPUs only`.\n- **Spread:** lower in 7 of 8 pairs.\n- **Median:** lower in 6 of 8 pairs, −0.33 s on average. The signs are not unanimous: this pod sits on a shared node and is noisy, so the latency gain is not established beyond \"usually faster, never much slower\".\n- **With mempolicy permitted:** on a whole-node 4x GB300 pod, main already binds, and this change takes the same path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format with pre-commit.\n- [x] Unit tests:\n  - `test/registered/utils/test_numa_utils.py` (CPU-only availability; memory policy skipped when not permitted, set when permitted);\n  - `test_gpu_worker_cpu_threads.py` (the worker binds without memory policy);\n  - 46 passed on the GB300 pod.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38200769648](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38200769648)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38200769499](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38200769499)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38200769737](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38200769737)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
